--TEST--
The entry answering an in-process request reads no listener of its own, so ADR 0079 § 18's two mechanisms do not reach each other
--FILE--
<?nvs
// § 18 has two mechanisms on purpose: the first runs this same entry over a
// synthetic request with no socket, the second binds one for a
// `#[Test(server: true)]` case. Neither is the other, and an address armed on
// the process rather than on a test's own context is exactly what would show
// up here — the re-entered entry would read one it was never given.
try {
    var $matched = Core\Request::route();
    if ($matched == null) {
        // Answering a request, so this `echo` is the response body (ADR 0088
        // § 3) and is read back below rather than printed here.
        echo "inside=", Core\Debug::render(Core\Test::serverUrl());
    }
} catch (LogicError $notARequest) {
    // The outer run: nothing is answering anything yet, so the entry is asked
    // for one request of its own.
    var $answered = Core\Test::request(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/anything");
    echo "outside=", Core\Debug::render(Core\Test::serverUrl()), "\n";
    echo $answered->body(), "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
outside=null
inside=null
